      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T04:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the whole file is loaded into memory, including the header. IIUC, text_offset\u003d0 means you are trying to execute the header\n\ni tried adding some padding and setting the offset, but it wasn\u0027t enough to get it working\n\n```\n--- a/guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py\n+++ b/guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ def append_arm64_header(original_kernel_file, text_offset, new_filename):\n     header_data \u003d {\n         \"code0\": 0,\n         \"code1\": 0,\n-        \"text_offset\": 0,\n+        \"text_offset\": 0x1000,\n         \"image_size\": len(original_data),\n         \"flags\": 0,\n         \"res2\": 0,\n@@ -75,6 +75,8 @@ def append_arm64_header(original_kernel_file, text_offset, new_filename):\n     # Write the header and original data to the new file\n     with open(new_filename, \"wb\") as f:\n         f.write(header_bytes)\n+        for i in range(0, 0x1000 - 64):\n+          f.write((0).to_bytes(1))\n         f.write(original_data)\n\n if __name__ \u003d\u003d \"__main__\":\n```",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dbdadb1_5168a425",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T04:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "oh, i had forgot about the idmap.S setup when i tried that. so, maybe pad to 2 mib of alignment here and then adjust the TEXT_ADDR to be `.ORIGIN_ADDR + (0 * .SZ_2M)`\n\nthat will waste a lot of space in the image file though. i wonder how linux kernel files handle this",
      "parentUuid": "0b0ba9de_8b8ef77f",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e2f5af3_84a07ba0",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T06:15:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e IIUC, text_offset\u003d0 means you are trying to execute the header\n\nI tried different offsets actually, that\u0027s indeed not enough to make it work. Otherwise I\u0027m not sure you need to handle the 64 bytes, since after the header parsing [1], the reading curser in `kernel_image` should be placed in the end of the header. So the next reading [2] will only take the original image.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/crosvm/kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs;l\u003d95;drc\u003d7d2280f04e0d3321fa35a63a855de325777def6d\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/crosvm/kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs;l\u003d107;drc\u003d7d2280f04e0d3321fa35a63a855de325777def6d",
      "parentUuid": "1dbdadb1_5168a425",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2a78c26_f8ae7e9d",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T17:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That tricked me too. It is using `read_at_*` (similar to `pread`) with an offset of zero, so the second read will read the header again.\n\nIt is more explicit in the `load_arm64_kernel_from_reader` version, where the header is written separately: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/crosvm/kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs;l\u003d132-135;drc\u003d7d2280f04e0d3321fa35a63a855de325777def6d",
      "parentUuid": "9e2f5af3_84a07ba0",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c193c44_66d97070",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
