      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T12:29:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s proceed with `bios` mode and the changes you suggested. That definitely looks simpler and quicker.\n\ncc @ptosi@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "f2a78c26_f8ae7e9d",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f605869_8e5093e9",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T13:20:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e IIUC, text_offset\u003d0 means you are trying to execute the header\n\nThat should work (by design), with any well-formed kernel header.\n\nFrom [`Documentation/arm64/booting.txt`](https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/arm64/booting.txt):\n```\nThe decompressed kernel image contains a 64-byte header as follows:\n\n  u32 code0;\t\t\t/* Executable code */\n  u32 code1;\t\t\t/* Executable code */\n  u64 text_offset;\t\t/* Image load offset, little endian */\n[...]\n- code0/code1 are responsible for branching to stext.\n```\nand see [`arch/arm64/kernel/head.S`](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/arch/arm64/kernel/head.S#61) for the code itself.\n\nThe following doesn\u0027t meet these requirements:\n```\n        \"code0\": 0,\n        \"code1\": 0,\n```",
      "parentUuid": "6c193c44_66d97070",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e1b46ff_56ae2320",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T14:21:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The following doesn\u0027t meet these requirements\n\nThese two fields are not used in crosvm:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/crosvm/kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs;l\u003d37;drc\u003d7d2280f04e0d3321fa35a63a855de325777def6d",
      "parentUuid": "6f605869_8e5093e9",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "408aa644_8fe27786",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T14:32:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, it doesn\u0027t change the fact that the header should be well-formed and executable. Those fields are not intended for the BL (VMM) but for the CPU (guest) to be executed as instructions.",
      "parentUuid": "6e1b46ff_56ae2320",
      "revId": "42586750992e4dd05fd95749860a59dc8a32018d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce11b7c4_563093e3",
        "filename": "guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T16:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh that is cool. I think as-is, this CL is shifting all the payload addresses around when it insert the header. Maybe if we could add the header with the help of the linker we could use that trick.\n\n\u003e Let\u0027s proceed with bios mode and the changes you suggested. That definitely looks simpler and quicker.\n\nSGTM",
